From: Peter Chiu <chui-hao.chiu@mediatek.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Jun 2025 13:26:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: remove the station BMC STA_REC on
 disconnection

A station link keeps its BMC STA_REC in the firmware after a
disconnection. The next association adds the same entry as new
again, and the entry then keeps the BSSID of the old AP. Commit
500c18014d95 ("mt76: mt7915: add sta_rec with EXTRA_INFO_NEW for the
first time only") also reports that the firmware can remove an entry
that is added as new twice.

Remove the BMC STA_REC when the BSSID of the link goes to zero on
disconnection. The next association then creates a new entry with
the new BSSID.

Signed-off-by: Peter Chiu <chui-hao.chiu@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/main.c |    4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -1010,6 +1010,10 @@ mt7996_link_info_changed(struct ieee8021
 	else if (changed & BSS_CHANGED_BSSID)
 		eth_zero_addr(link->bmc_bssid);
 
+	if (changed & BSS_CHANGED_BSSID && is_zero_ether_addr(info->bssid))
+		mt7996_mcu_add_sta(dev, info, NULL, link, &link->msta_link,
+				   CONN_STATE_DISCONNECT, false);
+
 	if (changed & BSS_CHANGED_HT || changed & BSS_CHANGED_ERP_CTS_PROT)
 		mt7996_mcu_set_protection(phy, link, info->ht_operation_mode,
 					  info->use_cts_prot);
